    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Wavelength $\\lambda = \\frac{v}{f} = \\frac{340}{500} = 0.68\\text{ m} = 68\\text{ cm}$. Resonances occur at $L_n = (2n - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{4} = (2n - 1)(17\\text{ cm})$. For $n=1$: $L_1 = 17\\text{ cm} < 100\\text{ cm}$. For $n=2$: $L_2 = 51\\text{ cm} < 100\\text{ cm}$. For $n=3$: $L_3 = 85\\text{ cm} < 100\\text{ cm}$. For $n=4$: $L_4 = 119\\text{ cm} > 100\\text{ cm}$. Thus exactly 3 resonances occur.",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "subject": "Physics",
    "class": "11",
    "chapter": "waves",
    "topicId": "phys-standing-waves",
    "subtopic": "Total Resonances in Draining Tube",
